[?2004l[?2004h> ## PAY-381 operations
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Webhook deliveries always require a valid `Paygate-Signature`, including retries.
[?2004l[?2004h> Replay-token headers do not bypass verification. Signature checks use the raw request
[?2004l[?2004h> bytes, the configured active secrets, and the configured timestamp tolerance. Event
[?2004l[?2004h> IDs are persisted so successful deliveries are not processed or audited again.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For trusted outage payloads already in `ops/backlog/`, use `npm run replay-backlog`.
[?2004l[?2004h> It skips processed event IDs and uses the same refund policy as the receiver. Keep
[?2004l[?2004h> payments on-call's refund-storm guard intact: at most 20 events per run, with at least
[?2004l[?2004h> 120 seconds between runs. Repeat after each interval until the command reports zero
[?2004l[?2004h> remaining events. This local recovery path does not require weakening HTTP signature
[?2004l[?2004h> verification or changing internal API permissions.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The approved policy auto-approves INR refunds up to and including ₹5,000 (500000
[?2004l[?2004h> minor units); larger refunds and all other currencies go to manual review.
